Declare the SIOCATMARK result as ULONG, the type p_ioctlsocket takes.

network.c declares ioctlsocket as taking ULONG * (its DECL_WINDOWS_FUNCTION)
but passes a u_long. Both are 32 bits on Windows, so the two agree there.
On an LP64 platform u_long is 64 bits and ULONG 32, so the pointer types
differ and the callee would write half the variable. ULONG is what the
declaration says, and is the same type on Windows. Line counts are
unchanged.

--- a/source/putty/windows/network.c	2026-10-11 18:40:03.028383533 -0300
+++ b/source/putty/windows/network.c	2026-10-11 18:40:03.032031213 -0300
@@ -1779,7 +1779,7 @@
          * (data prior to urgent).
          */
         if (s->oobinline) {
-            u_long atmark_from_ioctl = 1;
+            ULONG atmark_from_ioctl = 1;
             p_ioctlsocket(s->s, SIOCATMARK, &atmark_from_ioctl);
             /*
              * Avoid checking the return value from ioctlsocket(),
